---
title: Cauliflower Shaak
---

Cut @potato{1} and @cauliflower{1} into small pieces.

Heat @oil{4%tbsp} in a #pan or #wok on medium heat.

Add @hing{1/4%tsp} (asafetida), cut potatoes, and @water{3%tbsp}.

Cover the #pan and let it boil for ~{4%minutes}.

Add cauliflower pieces and @salt{1%tsp}.

Cover the #pan again to let it cook while tossing every ~{2%minutes}.

Once the contents have cooked, add @turmeric powder{1/4%tsp}, @dhanajiru powder{1%tbsp}, and @red chilli powder{1%tsp}.

Cover the #pot for another ~{4%minutes}.

Uncover, mix the contents and let it simmer for ~{2%minutes}.

Turn off the stove; the shaak should now be ready.
